From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NorkzYT <richard@pcscorp.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(kanban): typed dev_test_run tool that fails closed
 without an attested isolation backend, scanner recovery and test-credential
 guards

Neutralized derivative of `git diff 4f845b43ec..61cbead82d` of the runtime
branch feat/kanban-autonomous-reviewed: the added test fixtures use synthetic
names (profile example-service, module apps/example-service, database
example_test on 127.0.0.1:55432, EXAMPLE_TEST_DATABASE_URL, APP_DATABASE_URL)
instead of the original project's, and the diff was regenerated from a commit
of that neutralized tree, so index lines and hunks are genuine. Code paths
are unchanged. Upstream commits d15a70ddc8 (typed dev_test_run tool,
scanner recovery and test-credential guards), f04d4adc80 (fails closed on
rejected isolation, scoped recovery state, stricter target guard) and
61cbead82d (readiness needs an attested backend, not a mode string). The base
4f845b43ec is the third commit carried by 0003, so this patch contains no hunk
of 0001-0003 (the previous 0004 was cut against the wrong base and repeated
the agent/kanban_stop.py and tests/agent/test_kanban_stop.py hunks of 0003).

The registry must carry per-profile isolation.mode. `same-uid-landlock` is a
rejected design and `credential-broker-netns` is a recognised *proposed* design
string: syntactic config validity only. Runnable readiness needs
backend_attested() to pass, and no isolation backend is implemented, so at
every surface (tool visibility, RECOVERY directive, dev_test_run, kanban_block)
nothing is exposed regardless of what a root-owned registry declares; the
refusal names the missing implementation. The additive credential and file
guards read the trusted registry leniently so an older registry without
isolation.mode keeps blocking credential reads. Recovery state is scoped per
(task, run) and cleared only by an actual runner start or a recorded
precondition refusal. database_target_block covers ?host=, multi-host
authorities, hostaddr=, PGHOSTADDR and PGSERVICE* (text guard, not a
boundary). Result keys are redacted; the runner budget covers vet.

Tirith stays enabled and fail-closed, single-query/cron/unattended modes stay
deny, hardline and deny rules are unchanged.
